Boudewijn Waijers wrote on Thu, 9 Dec 2004 10:34:46 +0100:
> Rast wrote:
 
> > A proper nethack score system should be based on:
> > (for non-ascensions) progress made in the game
> > (for ascensions) turns used and conducts kept

> You do realise that the Dev Team, when they introduced conducts, have
> more than once commented that the conduct system is, and will remain,
> only optional, to accommodate those who think the game is too easy a
> little bit?

Casting "create monster" is optional.  But the current score system 
rewards it, almost to the exclusion of all other activities.

I didn't write, "players who have not kept at least three conducts 
shall be prohibited from ascending".  I simply suggested that for two 
similar ascensions, the one which has kept more/better conducts should 
be given a higher score.
 
> They have stated more than once that they have no intention at all to
> make it more important than that. Especially, they have stated that it
> will not be of influence on the scoring system, since they consider that
> conducts are only for *very* advanced players

As opposed to the only somewhat advanced players (see the recent 
dev/null tournament for examples) who spend X hundred thousand turns 
casting create monster near an altar before (optionally) ascending.

> So don't get your hopes up too high, except for the fact that you
> specifically mention "for ascensions", which might make a difference
> here. After all, those who manage to ascend may be considered advanced
> players...

I like this line of thought. :-)


